s fix round, the twin is the client: the evaluator is split into a store, a runner, and the entry and traces every point read with the digest of the wire row it disclosed, a hidden hit as an absence, and verdicts only from rule checks that disclosed their row (§6, §7); one schema and rule hasher mirrors serde's field order, refuses any field serde's struct does not carry, deep-sorts unknown variants, and the hydrate path recomputes the hash and refuses a mismatch (§6, §8); the program is held per generation beside the write bounds and re-fetched after `E_OFFLINE_RESET` (§6, §8); the drained-prefix rule is a chain of held pages on one (table, index, prefix, rule) from `after: null` to Exhausted, a page that lost a member since it was recorded is no link, and once Exhausted a page of the group holding a row the chain does not hold breaks it (§6); prediction runs inside the grant's critical section with the slice as its ids and lands overlay, trace, and `predicted` in the entry's own swap (§7); three deviations from "if every read is covered" are recorded: an uncovered range does not block a prediction, an unheld engine-maintained aggregate target does not block it and the omitted names ride the prediction, and a committed intent's overlay is dropped by an answer at or after the commit seq that touches one of its tables or any page of a drained op, never by an unrelated answer (§7); with a partition open every write carries the replay envelope or refuses `E_OFFLINE_ID_BLOCK` before any request, and only a client with no store sends plain bytes (§7); local authority violations are `E_OFFLINE_AUTHORITY` and keep coverage (§15); the IndexedDB `ranges`/`absences`/`verdicts` projections are gone (§6); the twin measures 19.7 KB gzip, engine alone 16.9 KB, and NOT-DOING's 9.7 KB is re-baselined to the measurement (§13, §14)); 2026-09-04 (f — implementation record, lanes O1b fix rounds 1–2, O2c, O4-web and its fix round, and the integration seams: grants are minted only when the request's `remaining` is absent or below 1,024 (§7, §8); the resume log op must be a certified ascending cursor page of at most 50 rows and its envelope counts against the 1 MiB budget (§8); the intent ledger is consulted before any grant check (§7); a replayed intent that rolls back on missing authority is stored as its partial terminal (§7); on the rejected path the compare set is every traced point plus every verdict a reached or probed rule check derived on a disclosed row, unreached verdicts re-derive only through the read rule, and the rule inputs a hidden candidate minted are excluded on both paths (§7); the verdict `inputsDigest` is `sha256(canonical([table, index, key]))` over wire values (§7); a replay needs a live session and the grant outlives the session (§7); the outbox's grant slice is `1 + maxNewIds` from the op's certificate, a transport failure keeps the intent queued and the retry is the same envelope, and a committed settlement lands in the same swap as the log tail (§7); `close()` resolves when the carrier is quiet (§6); asset bytes are keyed `(assetId, width|null)`, evicted least-recently-read by each entry's own stamp under the store's logical clock, and a view-once row is tracked per `(table, id)` in a durable viewed set, marked at the first byte fetch for an image and at play for a clip, read `null` on every path and excluded from coverage (§9); `E_ASSET_VIEWED` and `E_OFFLINE_CONFLICT` join the `offline` family (§15); `messages.send` stays in the template beside `deliveries.post` because a fixture pin holds `messages.q` byte-equal (§3); one open question for the author, the fence's local expiry of queued intents (§7)); 2026-09-04 (e — implementation record, lane O1b: grants are minted on every login, guest, and resume because the server cannot see the client's remaining count (§7); a trace conflict takes precedence over a program rejection, so a member removed while offline settles `conflict` rather than the program's own refusal (§7); the point digest is over the canonical wire row, which is what the pool carries (§7); an empty trace commits without a conflict check, which is the client's spelling until the twin lands (§7)); 2026-09-04 (d — implementation record, lanes O1a/O1c: the validator covers the row pool, `args`, `reason`, and `rule` (§8); row references carry engine provenance and application values are escaped (§8); `n2Key` is not on the wire; `GET /api/program` returns the schema; the recipe's tombstones reach current members and a departed member's copy is evicted by point absence, because the engine's uniformity analysis collects both arms of an `or` and Quarry cannot build a list from a range (§3); the membership cap is a maintained count (§3)); 2026-09-04 (c — the author's principle applied: the twin is the client from the start and stored-answer replay is its covered case (§6); intents carry the twin's trace and the server validates point reads and verdicts at commit (§7); the retention word ships as ruled, on the table whose rows can hide, with its twin-side meaning (§5); the bar gains one acceptance only the twin can pass (§12); lanes collapse to O1, O2, O4; (b)'s Q1–Q3 closed); 2026-09-04 (b — the panel's designs folded: positive-fact purge (tombstone rows, point absences, uniform-extent holes; no engine change), a frozen delivery envelope with one server-minted validator, resume as one owner action over the log's watermark plus mounted queries, a replay grant with an intent ledger for exactly-once, the corrected and certified recipe (page 50, `*`, a second log index for threads, compare-and-set edits), seal-not-wipe on session expiry, Web Locks across tabs, the journey primitives, the split witness, lane O3 off the bar's path pending ruling; §16 records who found what) (j — 2026-09-05: Status Implemented; the E2 witness record in §6)
